# Gaussian splat point clouds — capture OUTPUT, not source.
#
# These are the reconstructor's product and they are enormous: the three in the
# tree right now are 96 MB, 96 MB and 21 MB, which is 213 MB against GitHub's
# 100 MB per-file hard limit and a warning at 50 MB. They are also regenerable
# from the capture, so committing them would trade a permanent repo weight for
# something a re-run reproduces.
#
# The web app never needs one to work: components/relive probes the asset with a
# HEAD request and falls back to a synthetic point cloud badged `synthetic
# preview`, so a clean clone runs with none of these present. Drop a .ply into
# web/public/mock/splats/ locally and it renders for real.
#
# Ignored by extension rather than by directory so a stray capture anywhere in
# the tree is caught too. Sibling formats included — the pipeline emits .spz and
# some tools emit .splat/.ksplat.
*.ply
*.spz
*.splat
*.ksplat

# External tool, cloned locally (125GB nested git repo) — never vendor it
ComfyUI/
